     <item>
      <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="instructionsPlainTextEdit">
       <property name="font">
        <font>
         <italic>true</italic>
        </font>
       </property>
       <property name="plainText">
        <string>This import process loads, from an external file, a list of entries. Current entries will be deleted. This is useful when values are computed by an external model and entering them manually would be tedious. The file must be a Unicode-encoded text file (UTF-8, UTF-16 or UTF-32). Each line defines exactly one entry. Empty lines are not allowed. Format of each line: 

    &lt;date&gt;TAB&lt;growth&gt;

where

&lt;date&gt; : Transition date (first day the new value applies). ISO 8601 format: YYYY-MM-DD. E.g. 2025-01-01
TAB : Tab character (0x09)
&lt;growth&gt; : Annual growth (or inflation) rate in percentage, as a decimal number. Decimal separator must be .  E.g. 8.9234 means 8.9234%. Range: -100 to 10000. Up to 5 decimal places stored.

If two lines share the same date, the last one wins. </string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
